---
// walker.purr.io — the measurement report is the front door. The
// interactive demo lives at /live. Charts render client-side from
// site/src/data/measurement.json (built by `dog_walker.measure
// --build-report <archive...>`), so a re-run refreshes them by rebuild.
import data from "../data/measurement.json";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Which Model Walks the Dogs?</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/purrio_2026.png" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://walker.purr.io/" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A 210-run measurement of six small language models on a real tool-using dog-walking agent — pass rates with confidence intervals, real cost per plan, and how they fail."
    />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <nav class="topnav">
      <a class="logo" href="https://purr.io" aria-label="purr.io">
        <img src="/purrio_2026.png" alt="purr.io logo" />
      </a>
      <span class="brand">Agentic Dog Walker</span>
      <a href="/live">Run it live</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/rbhughes/agentic_dog_walker">GitHub</a>
      <span class="pill">measurement · 210 runs</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Model evaluation · 210 live runs</p>
      <h1>Which model walks the dogs?</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This is a measurement, and <strong>the measurement is the point</strong>
        — not the dog walking, and not any particular model. Of the cheap
        language models that can use tools and reason, which are actually good
        enough to run a real agent? The task below is only a yardstick, chosen
        because it has a <strong>deterministic finish line</strong>: a plan
        either passes the agent's own checks or it doesn't, so a score isn't a
        matter of opinion.
      </p>
      <p class="lede-2">
        The field is picked by rule, not taste. From OpenRouter's full catalog I
        keep only models that support tool calls and reasoning and are priced near
        the cheap end — at most $0.30 per million input tokens and $1.20 per
        million output — and each one has to clear a live end-to-end run to make
        the list, with a frontier model pinned in for contrast. Every survivor
        then plans the same dog walks below, using the same four real tools, and
        every plan is graded by the agent's checks rather than another model's.
      </p>
      <div class="herocta">
        <a class="cta" href="/live">Run the agent yourself →</a>
        <span class="ctahint">watch the live tool-calls at walker.purr.io/live</span>
      </div>

      <div class="statband">
        <div class="stat"><div class="k">{data.totals.runs}</div><div class="l">live runs, all paid</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="k">${data.totals.cost.toFixed(2)}</div><div class="l">total sweep cost</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="k">{data.totals.models}×{data.totals.scenarios}</div><div class="l">models × scenarios</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="k">k={data.totals.k}</div><div class="l">runs per cell</div></div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section id="task">
        <p class="eyebrow">The task being measured</p>
        <h2>An agent that plans dog walks — and can't fake it</h2>
        <p class="col">
          Give it a starting point and a few dogs, each with an address, a walk
          length, and constraints — a comfortable temperature band, a morning or
          afternoon window, hills to avoid, medication to administer. A small
          language model drives the whole thing: it geocodes the addresses, solves
          the visiting order over real streets, checks the weather for each dog's
          actual walk window, and returns a schedule with a per-dog safety verdict.
          It does that by calling four tools and relaying what they return.
        </p>
        <div class="toolgrid">
          <div class="tool">
            <span class="tname mono">geocode_addresses</span>
            <p>Street addresses → coordinates (Nominatim / OpenStreetMap).</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool">
            <span class="tname mono">check_weather</span>
            <p>Hourly forecast for a place and time window → a deterministic
              OK / CAUTION / SHORTEN / DO-NOT-WALK verdict.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool">
            <span class="tname mono">check_terrain</span>
            <p>Elevation around a dog's home → whether the hills exceed that
              dog's stated tolerance.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool">
            <span class="tname mono">optimize_route</span>
            <p>Real walking distances (OpenRouteService + OR-Tools) → the visiting
              order and a timed schedule; returns <span class="mono">feasible:false</span>
              when the windows can't all be met.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="col">
          The model is the least-trusted part of the system, and the measurement
          only works because it's boxed in. A <b>referee</b> validates every tool
          call against its schema before it runs. An <b>auditor</b> — plain code,
          no AI — refuses a finished plan unless every dog's walk has a real
          weather check at its own location. And the plan is submitted through a
          structured <span class="mono">submit_plan</span> whose validated
          arguments <em>are</em> the answer, never parsed from prose. Those checks
          are what make a "pass" mean something — the deterministic finish line a
          model can be measured against. <a href="/live">Watch it run live →</a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="verdict">
        <p class="eyebrow">The verdict</p>
        <h2>A $0.0004 model ties the frontier — and the model that looked worst was mostly our own bug.</h2>
        <p class="kicker">
          Two models finished all 35 runs, and the cheaper one — <b>66× cheaper</b> —
          is the new default. The bigger surprise came from the model that placed
          last in the first sweep: most of its failures weren't the model at all,
          but a bug in this harness. Fixing it moved the old default from 77% to 97%.
        </p>
        <div class="verdict">
          <div class="vcard win">
            <div class="tag">Best value · new default</div>
            <div class="model">inclusionai/ling-3.0-flash</div>
            <div class="figs">
              <div class="fig"><div class="n">100%</div><div class="u">35 / 35 passed</div></div>
              <div class="fig"><div class="n">$0.0004</div><div class="u">median / plan</div></div>
              <div class="fig"><div class="n">10s</div><div class="u">median</div></div>
            </div>
            <p>Perfect, fastest of the cheap tier, and the least expensive model
              in the sweep. Now the site default.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="vcard pricey">
            <div class="tag">Frontier baseline</div>
            <div class="model">anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5</div>
            <div class="figs">
              <div class="fig"><div class="n">100%</div><div class="u">35 / 35 passed</div></div>
              <div class="fig"><div class="n">$0.0265</div><div class="u">median / plan</div></div>
              <div class="fig"><div class="n">15s</div><div class="u">median</div></div>
            </div>
            <p>Also flawless — and it alone burned <b>70%</b> of the whole
              sweep's cost. The reliability is free; the certainty is not.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="vcard swap">
            <div class="tag">The harness's best catch</div>
            <div class="model">qwen/qwen3-8b</div>
            <div class="figs">
              <div class="fig"><div class="n">97%</div><div class="u">was 77%</div></div>
              <div class="fig"><div class="n">$0.0074</div><div class="u">median / plan</div></div>
              <div class="fig"><div class="n">54s</div><div class="u">median</div></div>
            </div>
            <p>It placed last in the first sweep. The harness traced the losses to
              our own referee rejecting <span class="mono">max_relief_m: 0</span> — the
              model's shorthand for "no hill limit." We fixed that; the re-run scores
              97%, one truncated response short of perfect. The bug was ours, not the
              model's. (Still not the default — ling is 18× cheaper.)</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="ranking">
        <p class="eyebrow">Reliability</p>
        <h2>Pass rate, with the doubt drawn in</h2>
        <p class="col">
          Five runs can't prove 100%. Each dot is the observed pass rate; the
          whisker is the <strong>95% Wilson interval</strong> — the honest
          range the true rate could sit in given only 35 samples. Note how wide
          even a perfect score's floor is, and how far the bottom two models'
          intervals reach.
        </p>
        <figure>
          <div class="chart-card">
            <p class="chart-title">Overall pass rate by model</p>
            <p class="chart-sub">35 runs per model · dot = observed rate, whisker = 95% CI</p>
            <div id="chart-rank"></div>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section id="cost">
        <p class="eyebrow">Cost vs. reliability</p>
        <h2>The frontier tax</h2>
        <p class="col">
          Plot what a plan costs against how often it lands and the trade-off
          stops being abstract. The <strong>upper-left</strong> is the prize:
          reliable and cheap. <span class="mono">ling-3.0-flash</span> sits
          there almost alone. <span class="mono">haiku-4.5</span> matches its
          reliability two orders of magnitude to the right.
        </p>
        <figure>
          <div class="chart-card">
            <p class="chart-title">Median cost per plan × pass rate</p>
            <p class="chart-sub">cost axis is logarithmic · each point is one model</p>
            <div id="chart-cost"></div>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section id="breakdown">
        <p class="eyebrow">Where they break</p>
        <h2>One scenario carries most of the difficulty</h2>
        <p class="col">
          Averages hide the shape of failure. Out of five runs per cell, the strong
          models are near-perfect except on one column: <strong>full-house</strong> —
          a single dog wearing every attribute at once (comfort band, meds, a morning
          window, prep time, and hills). <span class="mono">mercury-2.5</span> is the
          exception, thin across the board. And the first sweep's headline — the old
          default going <strong>0 for 5</strong> on Lakeview — is gone: that was the
          referee bug, now fixed, which is why qwen3-8b's row is almost solid green.
        </p>
        <div class="heat-scroll">
          <table class="heat" id="heat"></table>
        </div>
        <div class="heat-note">
          <span><span class="sw sw5"></span> 5/5 clean</span>
          <span><span class="sw sw4"></span> 3–4 / 5</span>
          <span><span class="sw sw2"></span> 1–2 / 5</span>
          <span><span class="sw sw0"></span> 0 / 5 — wholesale failure</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="taxonomy">
        <p class="eyebrow">How they fail</p>
        <h2>Not all failures are the model's fault</h2>
        <p class="col">
          Eighteen runs didn't pass, and lumping them into one number lies —
          they aren't the same kind of thing. The largest category in the first
          sweep, <strong>the referee being too strict</strong>, is gone entirely;
          fixing it is what recovered qwen3-8b. What's left is mostly
          infrastructure — a flaky provider, and long tool-call JSON that got
          truncated — plus a couple of genuine model mistakes.
        </p>
        <div class="tax" id="tax"></div>
        <div class="legend">
          <span><span class="sw swcomp"></span> the model's reasoning</span>
          <span><span class="sw swinfra"></span> infrastructure / provider</span>
        </div>

        <div class="callout">
          <h3>The one that matters: fabricated feasibility</h3>
          <p>Two runs, both from <span class="mono">mercury-2.5</span>, declared the
            <span class="mono">morning-overbook</span> roster <b>solvable</b>. It
            isn't: four hour-long walks that must all start before noon cannot be
            fit into one outing. The model called the route tool but <b>dropped
            the walk-window constraint</b>, so the deterministic tool saw an easy
            route and agreed.</p>
          <p>The in-loop auditor is blind here — it can only check the constraints
            the model actually passes. The measurement caught it anyway, because
            the harness knows the right answer independently. <b>That is the whole
            thesis:</b> you can measure an agent honestly only when the task has a
            checkable finish line the model can't talk its way past.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="callout warn">
          <h3>Reading the caveats honestly</h3>
          <p><b>mercury-2.5's</b> 71% is mostly an availability story: 8 of its
            losses were the provider returning no completion at all, not bad
            planning. <b>gpt-oss-120b's</b> dip to 86% is the same shape — a burst
            of malformed and truncated tool-call JSON on the heavier scenarios,
            not its planning; the <span class="mono">float(None)</span> bug that
            cost it two runs in the first sweep is fixed and gone. And the biggest
            correction is <b>qwen3-8b</b>: its first-sweep 77% was almost entirely
            our referee rejecting <span class="mono">max_relief_m: 0</span>. That's
            fixed, and the re-run confirms it — 34/35, a twenty-point jump. The
            lesson points back at the harness: a grader this strict catches your
            own bugs before it catches the model's.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="method">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it was measured</p>
        <h2>A grader that can't be charmed</h2>
        <p class="col">
          The task is dog-walk route planning: geocode addresses, solve the
          visiting order over real streets, check weather for each dog's actual
          walk window, respect terrain, medication, and comfort constraints, and
          finish with a structured plan. The numbers here combine the 2026-09-14
          sweep with a 2026-09-15 re-run of the two models whose failures the
          harness traced to bugs since fixed. <a href="/live">Try it live →</a>
        </p>
        <div class="method">
          <div>
            <h3><span class="step">01</span> Deterministic grade</h3>
            <p>A run passes iff it reaches a schema-validated
              <span class="mono">submit_plan</span> whose
              <span class="mono">feasible</span> flag matches the scenario's known
              answer. No model judges another. All seven scenarios' answers were
              checked against the solver before the sweep.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3><span class="step">02</span> Real cost &amp; latency</h3>
            <p>Dollars, not token estimates. Every model round's OpenRouter usage —
              prompt and completion tokens plus the actual charge — is summed per
              plan, so cost-per-run is measured, not modeled.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3><span class="step">03</span> Five runs, real intervals</h3>
            <p>Each of the 42 model×scenario cells runs five times. Pass rates carry
              a Wilson score interval, so "5/5" and "50/50" are never mistaken for
              the same confidence.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3><span class="step">04</span> Failures kept whole</h3>
            <p>Every failing run's full transcript is archived and sorted into a
              taxonomy from the event stream —
              <span class="taxa">veto_livelock, schema_thrash, prose_stall,
              fabricated_feasible, false_infeasible, backend_error, timeout</span>.
              The rejects are the content.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <p>
        Latest run {data.generated} · {data.totals.runs} runs · {data.totals.models} models ×
        {data.totals.scenarios} scenarios · k={data.totals.k} · ${data.totals.cost} ·
        harness <span class="mono">dog_walker.measure</span> · inference via OpenRouter.
      </p>
      <p class="colophon">A <a href="https://purr.io">purr.io</a> project · © 2026 · built in the open</p>
    </footer>

    <script define:vars={{ DATA: data }}>
      const MODELS = DATA.models;
      const PASS = "#4a6fa5", POOR = "#cc6137";      // reliable vs poor (CVD-safe blue/terracotta)
      const tone = m => (m.pass / m.n >= 0.90 ? PASS : POOR);
      const SVGNS = "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg";
      function el(tag, attrs, text) {
        const n = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);
        for (const k in attrs) n.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);
        if (text != null) n.textContent = text;
        return n;
      }

      /* pass-rate ranking with Wilson whiskers */
      (function rank() {
        const rows = MODELS.slice().sort((a, b) => b.pass - a.pass || a.cost - b.cost);
        const W = 860, rowH = 48, padT = 24, padB = 34, padL = 168, padR = 128;
        const H = padT + rows.length * rowH + padB;
        const x0 = padL, x1 = W - padR, dmin = 0.45;
        const sx = v => x0 + (v - dmin) / (1 - dmin) * (x1 - x0);
        const svg = el("svg", { viewBox:`0 0 ${W} ${H}`, role:"img",
          "aria-label":"Pass rate by model with 95% confidence intervals" });
        for (let t = 0.5; t <= 1.001; t += 0.1) {
          const x = sx(t);
          svg.appendChild(el("line", { x1:x, x2:x, y1:padT-6, y2:H-padB, class:"grid" }));
          svg.appendChild(el("text", { x, y:H-padB+18, "text-anchor":"middle", class:"tk" }, Math.round(t*100)+"%"));
        }
        rows.forEach((m, i) => {
          const cy = padT + i*rowH + rowH/2, rate = m.pass/m.n, color = tone(m);
          const lo = sx(m.ci[0]), hi = sx(m.ci[1]);
          // faint row guide, then the 95% CI whisker, then the dot on top
          svg.appendChild(el("line", { x1:x0, x2:x1, y1:cy, y2:cy, stroke:"var(--surface-2)", "stroke-width":1 }));
          svg.appendChild(el("line", { x1:lo, x2:hi, y1:cy, y2:cy, stroke:"var(--ink)", "stroke-width":2, opacity:0.3 }));
          [lo, hi].forEach(xx => svg.appendChild(el("line", { x1:xx, x2:xx, y1:cy-5, y2:cy+5, stroke:"var(--ink)", "stroke-width":2, opacity:0.3 })));
          svg.appendChild(el("circle", { cx:sx(rate), cy:cy, r:7, fill:color, stroke:"var(--surface)", "stroke-width":2 }));
          svg.appendChild(el("text", { x:x0-14, y:cy+1, "text-anchor":"end", class:"lbl", "dominant-baseline":"middle" }, m.short));
          if (m.note) svg.appendChild(el("text", { x:x0-14, y:cy+15, "text-anchor":"end", class:"lbl-2", "dominant-baseline":"middle" }, m.note));
          svg.appendChild(el("text", { x:hi+12, y:cy+1, class:"val", "dominant-baseline":"middle" }, Math.round(rate*100)+"%   "+m.pass+"/"+m.n));
        });
        svg.appendChild(el("line", { x1:x0, x2:x1, y1:H-padB, y2:H-padB, class:"ax" }));
        document.getElementById("chart-rank").appendChild(svg);
      })();

      /* cost vs reliability scatter */
      (function cost() {
        const W = 860, H = 470, padT = 26, padB = 56, padL = 66, padR = 34;
        const x0 = padL, x1 = W - padR, y0 = H - padB, y1 = padT;
        const cmin = 0.0003, cmax = 0.03, lx = v => Math.log10(v);
        const sx = v => x0 + (lx(v)-lx(cmin))/(lx(cmax)-lx(cmin)) * (x1-x0);
        const ymin = 0.68, ymax = 1.005, sy = v => y0 - (v-ymin)/(ymax-ymin) * (y0-y1);
        const svg = el("svg", { viewBox:`0 0 ${W} ${H}`, role:"img",
          "aria-label":"Median cost per plan versus pass rate" });
        for (let t = 0.7; t <= 1.001; t += 0.1) {
          const y = sy(t);
          svg.appendChild(el("line", { x1:x0, x2:x1, y1:y, y2:y, class:"grid" }));
          svg.appendChild(el("text", { x:x0-12, y:y+4, "text-anchor":"end", class:"tk" }, Math.round(t*100)+"%"));
        }
        [0.0005,0.001,0.002,0.005,0.01,0.02].forEach(v => {
          const x = sx(v);
          svg.appendChild(el("line", { x1:x, x2:x, y1:y1-4, y2:y0, class:"grid" }));
          svg.appendChild(el("text", { x, y:y0+18, "text-anchor":"middle", class:"tk" }, "$"+v));
        });
        svg.appendChild(el("text", { x:(x0+x1)/2, y:H-14, "text-anchor":"middle", class:"lbl-2" }, "median cost per plan  (log scale)"));
        svg.appendChild(el("text", { x:16, y:(y0+y1)/2, "text-anchor":"middle", class:"lbl-2", transform:`rotate(-90 16 ${(y0+y1)/2})` }, "pass rate"));
        const LAB = {
          "ling-3.0-flash": { dx:16,  dy:5,  anc:"start" },
          "haiku-4.5":      { dx:-16, dy:5,  anc:"end" },
          "qwen3.7-flash":  { dx:0,   dy:30, anc:"middle" },
          "gpt-oss-120b":   { dx:16,  dy:5,  anc:"start" },
          "qwen3-8b":       { dx:16,  dy:5,  anc:"start" },
          "mercury-2.5":    { dx:-16, dy:5,  anc:"end" },
        };
        MODELS.forEach(m => {
          const p = LAB[m.short] || { dx:16, dy:5, anc:"start" };
          const x = sx(m.cost), y = sy(m.pass/m.n), tx = x + p.dx;
          svg.appendChild(el("text", { x:tx, y:y+p.dy-8, "text-anchor":p.anc, class:"lbl" }, m.short));
          svg.appendChild(el("text", { x:tx, y:y+p.dy+6, "text-anchor":p.anc, class:"lbl-2" },
            "$"+m.cost.toFixed(4)+"  /  "+Math.round(m.pass/m.n*100)+"%"));
          svg.appendChild(el("circle", { cx:x, cy:y, r:9, fill:tone(m), stroke:"var(--surface)", "stroke-width":2.5 }));
        });
        svg.appendChild(el("line", { x1:x0, x2:x1, y1:y0, y2:y0, class:"ax" }));
        svg.appendChild(el("line", { x1:x0, x2:x0, y1:y0, y2:y1, class:"ax" }));
        document.getElementById("chart-cost").appendChild(svg);
      })();

      /* heatmap */
      (function heat() {
        const scenarios = DATA.scenarios;
        const cls = v => v===5?"c5":v>=3?"c4":v>=1?"c2":"c0";
        const t = document.getElementById("heat");
        const thead = document.createElement("thead"), hr = document.createElement("tr");
        hr.appendChild(document.createElement("th"));
        scenarios.forEach(s => { const th = document.createElement("th"); th.innerHTML = s.replace("-","-<br>"); hr.appendChild(th); });
        thead.appendChild(hr); t.appendChild(thead);
        const tb = document.createElement("tbody");
        DATA.models.forEach(m => {
          const tr = document.createElement("tr");
          const th = document.createElement("th"); th.className="rowh"; th.textContent=m.short; tr.appendChild(th);
          m.cells.forEach(v => { const td = document.createElement("td"); td.className=cls(v); td.textContent=v; td.title=m.short+": "+v+"/"+(m.n/scenarios.length); tr.appendChild(td); });
          tb.appendChild(tr);
        });
        t.appendChild(tb);
      })();

      /* failure taxonomy */
      (function tax() {
        // outcome -> (bar colour class, plain-language cause)
        const KIND = {
          backend_error:       ["infra",  "provider / our-bug"],
          schema_thrash:       ["strict", "referee too strict"],
          fabricated_feasible: ["comp",   "model reasoning"],
          false_infeasible:    ["comp",   "model reasoning"],
          timeout:             ["comp",   "model reasoning"],
          veto_livelock:       ["comp",   "model reasoning"],
          prose_stall:         ["comp",   "model reasoning"],
          no_submit:           ["comp",   "model reasoning"],
        };
        const rows = DATA.taxonomy;
        if (!rows.length) { document.getElementById("taxonomy").style.display = "none"; return; }
        const max = Math.max.apply(null, rows.map(r => r.n));
        const host = document.getElementById("tax");
        rows.forEach(r => {
          const [cls, label] = KIND[r.name] || ["comp", "model reasoning"];
          const row = document.createElement("div");
          row.className = "taxrow " + cls;
          row.innerHTML =
            `<div class="name">${r.name}<div class="kind">${label}</div></div>` +
            `<div class="bar"><div class="fill" style="width:${(r.n/max*100).toFixed(1)}%">${r.n}</div></div>`;
          host.appendChild(row);
        });
      })();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  :root {
    --page: #f3f4f6;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --surface-2: #eef0f3;
    --ink: #262e42;
    --ink-2: #5b6577;
    --muted: #9aa0ab;
    --hairline: #dfe1e6;
    --border: rgba(38, 46, 66, 0.12);
    --accent: #4a6fa5;
    --brand: #cc6137;
    --gold: #eeb63f;
    --track: #e7e9ee;
    --ok: #2f7d33;
    --caution: #b26a00;
    --danger: #990000;
    /* heatmap tints (bg / text) */
    --c5-bg: #e4ecf5; --c5-fg: #3a5f96;
    --c4-bg: #f7ead0; --c4-fg: #9a6a12;
    --c2-bg: #f6ddd3; --c2-fg: #b8481f;
    --c0-bg: #f3d2d2; --c0-fg: #990000;
    --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(38,46,66,.05), 0 10px 28px rgba(38,46,66,.07);
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0; min-height: 100vh; display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    background: var(--page); color: var(--ink);
    font: 16px/1.62 Poppins, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  a { color: var(--accent); text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .mono { font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace; }
  .wrap, main { max-width: 840px; }
  main { margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; width: 100%; }
  /* paragraphs fill the same column as the cards and charts, so nothing
     reads as inset or off-centre */
  .col { max-width: none; }

  /* top nav — family chrome */
  .topnav {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.7rem;
    padding: 0.55rem 2.1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    background: var(--surface); flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .topnav .logo img { height: 26px; width: 26px; display: block; border-radius: 6px; }
  .topnav .brand { font-weight: 700; color: var(--brand); margin-right: 0.3rem; }
  .topnav a { text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.92rem; font-weight: 500; }
  .topnav a[href="/live"] { color: var(--brand); font-weight: 600; }
  .pill {
    margin-left: auto; font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--ink-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.7rem; background: var(--page);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--brand); margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  h1, h2, h3 { font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; text-wrap: balance; margin: 0; }

  /* hero */
  .hero {
    max-width: 840px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 60px 24px 44px; width: 100%;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 6vw, 3.8rem); line-height: 1.03; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0; }
  .lede strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .lede-2 { font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--ink-2); margin: 16px 0 0; }
  .herocta { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 30px; }
  .cta {
    display: inline-block; background: var(--brand); color: #fff;
    font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; padding: 0.7rem 1.3rem;
    border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: var(--shadow); transition: transform .12s ease, background .12s ease;
  }
  .cta:hover { background: #b5501f; transform: translateY(-1px); }
  .ctahint { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); }

  .statband {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 1px; margin-top: 40px;
    background: var(--border); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .stat { background: var(--surface); padding: 18px 20px; }
  .stat .k { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .stat .l { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 2px; }

  section { padding: 52px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.4vw, 2.2rem); line-height: 1.12; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  p { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  p.col, .kicker { color: var(--ink-2); }
  p.col strong, .kicker b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .kicker { font-size: 1.06rem; }

  /* tool grid (the explainer) */
  .toolgrid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 14px; margin: 24px 0; }
  .tool { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 16px 18px; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .tool .tname { display:block; font-size: .92rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 5px; }
  .tool p { margin: 0; font-size: .9rem; color: var(--ink-2); }

  /* verdict cards */
  .verdict { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 26px; }
  .vcard {
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 22px; box-shadow: var(--shadow); position: relative; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .vcard::before { content:""; position:absolute; inset:0 auto 0 0; width:5px; background: var(--muted); }
  .vcard.win::before { background: var(--ok); }
  .vcard.pricey::before { background: var(--gold); }
  .vcard.swap::before { background: var(--brand); }
  .vcard .tag { font-size:11px; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.08em; color: var(--muted); }
  .vcard.win .tag { color: var(--ok); }
  .vcard.pricey .tag { color: var(--caution); }
  .vcard.swap .tag { color: var(--brand); }
  .vcard .model { font-weight:700; font-size:1rem; margin: 8px 0 12px; word-break: break-all; font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
  .vcard .figs { display:flex; gap: 20px; }
  .vcard .fig .n { font-weight:800; font-size:1.25rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .vcard .fig .u { font-size:11.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  .vcard p { font-size: .92rem; color: var(--ink-2); margin: 14px 0 0; }

  /* charts */
  figure { margin: 26px 0 0; }
  .chart-card { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 24px 26px 20px; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .chart-title { font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0 0 2px; }
  .chart-sub { font-size: .88rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 18px; }
  svg { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; overflow:visible; }
  .ax { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width:1; }
  .grid { stroke: var(--surface-2); stroke-width:1; }
  .tk { font-size:11px; fill: var(--muted); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
  .lbl { font-size:12.5px; fill: var(--ink); font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
  .lbl-2 { font-size:11.5px; fill: var(--muted); }
  .val { font-size:12.5px; font-weight:600; fill: var(--ink); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }

  .legend { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:16px; margin-top:18px; font-size:12.5px; color:var(--ink-2); }
  .legend span { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:7px; }
  .sw { width:13px; height:13px; border-radius:3px; display:inline-block; }
  .sw5 { background: var(--ok); } .sw4 { background: var(--caution); }
  .sw2 { background: var(--brand); } .sw0 { background: var(--danger); }
  .swcomp { background: var(--brand); } .swstrict { background: var(--caution); } .swinfra { background: var(--muted); }

  /* heatmap */
  .heat-scroll { overflow-x: auto; margin-top: 22px; }
  table.heat { border-collapse: separate; border-spacing: 4px; min-width: 640px; }
  table.heat th { font-weight:500; font-size:11.5px; color: var(--muted); padding: 0 4px 8px;
    vertical-align: bottom; text-align: center; line-height:1.25; }
  table.heat th.rowh { text-align: right; font-weight:700; color: var(--ink); font-size:12.5px;
    padding-right: 12px; white-space: nowrap; font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
  table.heat td { width: 62px; height: 44px; text-align:center; border-radius: 8px; font-weight:700;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-size: 14px; font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
  td.c5 { background: var(--c5-bg); color: var(--c5-fg); }
  td.c4 { background: var(--c4-bg); color: var(--c4-fg); }
  td.c2 { background: var(--c2-bg); color: var(--c2-fg); }
  td.c0 { background: var(--c0-bg); color: var(--c0-fg); }
  .heat-note { display:flex; gap:18px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:16px; font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); }

  /* taxonomy */
  .tax { margin-top: 24px; display: grid; gap: 14px; }
  .taxrow { display:grid; grid-template-columns: 190px 1fr; gap: 18px; align-items:center; }
  .taxrow .name { font-size:.9rem; color:var(--ink); text-align:right; font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
  .taxrow .kind { font-size:10.5px; letter-spacing:.03em; text-transform:uppercase; color: var(--muted); font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; }
  .taxrow .bar { position: relative; height: 30px; background: var(--surface-2); border-radius: 7px; overflow: hidden; }
  .taxrow .fill { position:absolute; inset:0 auto 0 0; border-radius:7px; display:flex; align-items:center;
    padding-left: 11px; color:#fff; font-weight:700; font-size:13px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .infra .fill { background: var(--muted); } .strict .fill { background: var(--caution); } .comp .fill { background: var(--brand); }

  .callout { margin: 26px 0 0; padding: 22px 24px; border-radius: 14px; background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 5px solid var(--accent); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .callout.warn { border-left-color: var(--caution); }
  .callout h3 { color: var(--accent); }
  .callout.warn h3 { color: var(--caution); }
  .callout p { color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0; }
  .callout p + p { margin-top: 12px; }

  .method { display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr); gap: 30px 40px; margin-top: 24px; }
  .method h3 { display:flex; align-items:baseline; gap:10px; }
  .method h3 .step { font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; font-size:12px; color:var(--brand); font-weight:700; }
  .method p { font-size:.95rem; color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0; }
  .taxa { font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; font-size:.8rem; }

  footer { margin-top: auto; padding: 34px 24px 48px; max-width: 840px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; width: 100%; }
  footer p { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0.35rem 0; }
  footer .colophon { color: var(--ink-2); }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .statband { grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr); }
    .verdict, .method { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .taxrow { grid-template-columns: 130px 1fr; }
    .topnav { padding: 0.55rem 1.1rem; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .cta { transition: none; } }
</style>
